r. Not capsid.\n\nAlso, **\"Delaware Biotech Institute\"**? Not needed.\n\nBetter candidates aligned to \"capsid–receptor complex modeling for BBB transcytosis in BMEC\":\n1. Gradinaru Lab (Caltech) — APPRAISE + PHP.eB/PHP.eC/CA4 engineering. Direct.\n2. Dyno Therapeutics — capsid AI + partners (Novartis CNS, Sarepta muscle, Roche?). Their published work (Bryant et al. 2021 Nat Biotechnol with Caskey/Gradinaru? no, Bryant was Caltech). Dyno's \"Nature Communications 2025: machine learning...\". They do use structural/biophysical modeling? Need to check their site.\n3. Capsida Biotherapeutics — \"engineered capsids that cross the BBB\"; their platform includes \"capsid engineering with structural insights\"; partnered with Lilly (2021) and AbbVie (2024?) for CNS and eye. Active.\n\nOr maybe a European consortium: \"BRAINAV\"? Hmm.\n\nAlso open-source: \"ColabFold\" or \"AF-Multimer benchmarking\"? Or \"AAV capsid database (AAVid / AAV Atlas)\"? The card's result would feed an open-source project like **APPRAISE itself** (GradinaruLab/APPRAISE on GitHub) — that's the most direct. But \"programmes... doing this work now\" — APPRAISE is a tool project.\n\nI think the best 1-3:\n1. Gradinaru Lab (Caltech) — APPRAISE-AAV pipeline (exact step: AF-Multimer capsid-peptide/receptor complex ranking).\n2. Dyno Therapeutics — capsid engineering with ML + structural work for CNS (Novartis partnership).\n3. Capsida Biotherapeutics — BBB-crossing capsid engineering for CNS programs.\n\nLet me gather evidence for each: step description in their own words with quotes, activity (recent release/commit/paper), practice implications, already-done check.\n\nAlso check: has anyone already run this experiment (exhaustive pose sampling / shared 3-fold GPI motif across a capsid panel)? The Shay 2023 paper used 10 models per competition and had false negatives; the Ding 2024 paper (Mol Ther) has APPRAISE details; also there may be a paper on \"PHP.eB-LY6A complex structure\" (Jang 2022, cryo-E