    "reasoning_content": "Excellent. Now I have three strong programmes:\n\n1. **Gradinaru Lab (Caltech) — APPRAISE-AAV / open-source APPRAISE package**: direct origin of the method. Step: ranking capsid peptides against receptors by AF-Multimer pose scoring (pairwise competitions, 10 models each) as a pre-screen. Activity: active — commits Apr 9, 2026 (\"Colab instruction update\", \"distribution 1.2.6\" / \"1.3.0 package\", Boltz-1/Chai-1/OpenFold3 support). URL: https://github.com/GradinaruLab/APPRAISE. Step quote from README: \"APPRAISE... predicts the receptor binding propensity of engineered proteins based on high-precision protein structure prediction tools, such as AlphaFold2-multimer.\" Or from Shay 2023 methods: \"Each model was recycled three times, and 10 models were generated from each competition.\"\n\n2. **Dyno Therapeutics**: BBB-crossing capsid portfolio (Dyno-9zh ALPL, Dyno-yp2 TfR1, Dyno-ahq, Dyno-hc9) with \"sequence- and structure-based approaches to engineer functional capsids for new and promising BBB-crossing mechanisms\". The card's phenotype labels reference ALPL. Activity: active — Dyno-yp2 launched Jan 12, 2026, Dyno-9zh launched 2026. Also the card's \"s_alpl\" is likely Dyno's ALPL capsid work. This is the industrial programme that most directly needs \"which capsid-receptor binding signatures mark transcytosis vs intracellular retention\".\n\n3. **Capsida Biotherapeutics**: \"Identification of Multiple Novel Blood-Brain Barrier Receptors... via an Integrated AAV Capsid Engineering Platform\" (ASGCT May 2025); \"We have identified novel human blood-brain barrier receptors that bind our engineered capsids and are conserved between primates and humans\"; \"In Vitro Binding Platform Demonstrates Reproducible Capsid/Receptor Binding Data Consistent with Expression Profiles\" — NR001-005, NR004 endothelial-specific. Their step: capsid/receptor binding characterization (plate-based and bead-based receptor binding detection), deciding which ca