    "content": "Dyno | Gene Delivery  \n\n[](/)\n\n-   [Gene Delivery](/gene-delivery)\n-   [Partnership](/partnerships)\n-   [Approach](/approach)\n-   [About](/about)\n-   [News](/news)\n-   [Blog](https://dynotx.substack.com/)\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/66f5d651201ba55986e2fe12/67d8920cf1179e16a6b9b764_mobile-nav-bg-noise.png)\n\nMenu\n\nClose\n\ngene delivery\n\n# Deliver with confidence\n\nDyno’s capsid technology enables gene therapy developers to target the brain, eye and muscle with field-leading performance.\n\n-   Brain\n    \n    [\n    \n    Dyno-9zh\n    \n    ](/gene-delivery#Dyno-9zh)[\n    \n    Dyno-yp2\n    \n    ](/gene-delivery#Dyno-yp2)[\n    \n    Dyno-ahq\n    \n    ](/gene-delivery#Dyno-ahq)[\n    \n    Dyno-hc9\n    \n    ](/gene-delivery#Dyno-hc9)\n    \n-   Muscle/Neuromuscular\n    \n    [\n    \n    Dyno-bn8\n    \n    ](/gene-delivery#Dyno-bn8)\n    \n    [\n    \n    Dyno-n96\n    \n    ](/gene-delivery#Dyno-n96)\n    \n    [\n    \n    Dyno-3hv\n    \n    ](/gene-delivery#Dyno-3hv)\n    \n-   Eye\n    \n    [\n    \n    Dyno-4z2\n    \n    ](/gene-delivery#Dyno-4z2)[\n    \n    Dyno-86m\n    \n    ](/gene-delivery#Dyno-86m)\n    \n\nBrain\n\n[\n\nDyno-9zh\n\n](/gene-delivery#Dyno-9zh)\n\n[\n\nDyno-yp2\n\n](/gene-delivery#Dyno-yp2)\n\n[\n\nDyno-ahq\n\n](/gene-delivery#Dyno-ahq)\n\n[\n\nDyno-hc9\n\n](/gene-delivery#Dyno-hc9)\n\nMuscle/ Neuromuscular\n\n[\n\nDyno-bn8\n\n](/gene-delivery#Dyno-bn8)\n\n[\n\nDyno-n96\n\n](/gene-delivery#Dyno-n96)\n\n[\n\nDyno-3hv\n\n](/gene-delivery#Dyno-3hv)\n\nEYE\n\n[\n\nDyno-4z2\n\n](/gene-delivery#Dyno-4z2)\n\n[\n\nDyno-86m\n\n](/gene-delivery#Dyno-86m)\n\nBrain\n\n## Dyno-9zh\n\nLaunched in 2026, the Dyno-9zh is a top-performing capsid that achieves both exceptional brain transduction with significant liver detargeting in NHPs and mouse.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a0249899d5983c3ff528ebc_Dyno-yp2-capsid.png)\n\nLaunched in 2026, the Dyno-9zh is a top-performing capsid that achieves both exceptional brain transduction with significant liver detargeting in NHPs and mouse.\n\n[\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a027811eafda6d965183fd1_Group%201538240438.webp)\n\nExpand Image\n\n](#)\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024a025e1ff3b983b95bab_Group%201538240410.svg)\n\n**Crosses BBB** reaching up to **50%** of neurons in the NHP cortex at a dose of 3e13 vg/kg.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024a0834d7890f9169cb5d_Icons.svg)\n\n**Exceptional liver detargeting** in mouse and NHP, with **\\>10x** lower biodistribution than AAV9.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024a0b4097b23f2d561e03_6962122362a4b74e399b8a8b_bar-chart%201.svg)\n\nBest **capsid when compared head-to-head** with other ALPL-targeting capsids in mouse and NHP.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024a0e0987ecacd9f6c3c8_681e2c34cc117d9f87a1a80f_Icons%20from%20Figma%20(1)%201.svg)\n\nEngages **human Alkaline Phosphatase (ALPL)** receptor for BBB-crossing, supporting **translation to humans.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024a101b6b0b38e86f9b64_Icons-1.svg)\n\nAvailable for large-scale manufacturing, ensuring clinical comparability and predictability.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a075e5ba00d4e02168423e4_Group%201538240638.png)[View Presentation](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a0643626a1c6767048a91ca_Dyno-9zh_slides.pdf)\n\nBrain\n\n## Dyno-yp2\n\nLaunched in 2026, the Dyno-yp2 is a top-performing capsid that achieves both exceptional brain transduction in humanized TfR mice and significant liver detargeting.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/69621082a1224b0df41bc1c4_Dyno-yp2-capsid.png)\n\nLaunched in 2026, the Dyno-yp2 is a top-performing capsid that achieves both exceptional brain transduction in humanized TfR mice and significant liver detargeting.\n\n[\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/696213537e331b216df6c8e4_Dyno-yp2-histology%20(2)%20(1).jpg)\n\nExpand Image\n\n](#)\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2d5f2cc9592ca32244d6_Icons%20from%20Figma%20(2).svg)\n\n**Crosses BBB** reaching up to **93%** of neurons in humanized TfR1 mice at a dose of 2e13 vg/kg, with **113x** higher brain transduction vs AAV9.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2c452cc9592ca321a996_Group.svg)\n\n**Exceptional liver detargeting in both mice and NHPs,** with **29x** lower biodistribution than AAV9.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6962122362a4b74e399b8a8b_bar-chart.svg)\n\n**Outperforms** BI-hTFR1 and BI-hTFR1-v2 in brain transduction in humanized TfR1 mice.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2c34cc117d9f87a1a80f_Icons%20from%20Figma%20(1).svg)\n\nEngages highly conserved human transferrin receptor (hTfR) **receptor** for BBB-crossing, supporting **translation to humans.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6834c26dd42148723c30e214_gear.svg)\n\nAvailable for large-scale manufacturing, ensuring clinical comparability and predictability.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a075e9655ac07b4240e4e4c_Group%201538240639.png)[View Presentation](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a0642f4335a4fa036c08d4b_Dyno-yp2_slides.pdf)\n\nBrain\n\n## Dyno-ahq\n\nLaunched in 2025, the Dyno-ahq capsid is optimized for widespread IV delivery to the brain, with exceptional liver detargeting and a highly conserved mechanism for blood-brain barrier crossing.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2d238f5373893e796b34_Group%20Design.png)\n\nLaunched in 2025, the Dyno-ahq capsid is optimized for widespread IV delivery to the brain, with exceptional liver detargeting and a highly conserved mechanism for blood-brain barrier crossing.\n\n[\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/69129e99b396e18a9cbfe8ec_dyno-ahq_Slab4-whole_highres%201.png)\n\nExpand Image\n\n](#)\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2d5f2cc9592ca32244d6_Icons%20from%20Figma%20(2).svg)\n\n**Crosses BBB** reaching up to **30%** of NHP neurons at a dose of 3e13 vg/kg, with **280x** higher brain transduction vs AAV9.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2c452cc9592ca321a996_Group.svg)\n\n**50x** lower liver transduction compared to AAV9.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2d2f919034e63f0bbedf_Icons%20from%20Figma.svg)\n\n**Intravenous** injection enables more uniform brain transduction and **broader patient access.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2d3b32a0a2cd53dc3db3_Icons%20from%20Figma%20(1).svg)\n\nOptimized and validated in **NHPs.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2c34cc117d9f87a1a80f_Icons%20from%20Figma%20(1).svg)\n\nHighly conserved **candidate receptor** for BBB-crossing supports **translation to humans.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/69c198b27a14c4963f02b572_Group%201538240638.png)[View Presentation](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6823a5fac9d16405d6f514ed_Web%20upload%20-%20ASGCT25%20Dyno-ahq.pdf)\n\nBrain\n\n## Dyno-hc9\n\nLaunched in 2023, the Dyno-hc9 capsid (aka bCap 1) was the first Dyno capsid optimized for highly efficient delivery across the blood-brain barrier, with broad CNS tropism and liver detargeting.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2e41f6f25cffec75369b_Group%20Design.png)\n\nLaunched in 2023, the Dyno-hc9 capsid (aka bCap 1) was the first Dyno capsid optimized for highly efficient delivery across the blood-brain barrier, with broad CNS tropism and liver detargeting.\n\n[\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/69129e7f9dc9915ae7393f63_dyno-hc9_Slab5-whole_highres_bc%201.png)\n\nExpand Image\n\n](#)\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6834c26dd42148723c30e214_gear.svg)\n\n**100x** higher brain transduction and **10x** lower liver transduction vs. AAV9, with **similar production efficiency.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2d62ba4f2c8098683d52_Layer%201.svg)\n\nTransduces neurons and glia, including cell-types relevant for **ALS, Huntington’s, Parkinson’s Disease.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2d5f2cc9592ca32244d6_Icons%20from%20Figma%20(2).svg)\n\nReaches **deep brain regions** and the **spinal cord.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2d2f919034e63f0bbedf_Icons%20from%20Figma.svg)\n\nEasy **intravenous** injection enables uniform transduction and **broad patient access.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2d3b32a0a2cd53dc3db3_Icons%20from%20Figma%20(1).svg)\n\nOptimized and validated in **NHPs.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/69c198cfe38dceb1878b5830_hc9.png)[View Presentation](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e5d745e00412092803046_bCap-Factsheet_compressed%20\\(1\\).pdf)\n\nMuscle/Neuromuscular\n\n## Dyno-bn8\n\nLaunched in 2025, the Dyno-bn8 capsid enables therapeutic delivery to skeletal and cardiac muscles at IV doses as low as 5e12 vg/kg, dramatically improving safety for muscle and neuromuscular gene therapies.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/69127d1db198c92f26229a20_Group%201538240398.png)\n\nLaunched in 2025, the Dyno-bn8 capsid enables therapeutic delivery to skeletal and cardiac muscles at IV doses as low as 5e12 vg/kg, dramatically improving safety for muscle and neuromuscular gene therapies.\n\n[\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024b80eac1dce44c7db786_Group%201538240438%20(1).webp)\n\nExpand Image\n\n](#)\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/69127bc542c576664baf453a_Icons-2.svg)\n\nEven at the low dose of 5e12 vg/kg (25x lower dose than Elevidys), transduces **73-88% of myofibers** in NHP skeletal muscles.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/69127bc96eebb67f365ae271_Icons.svg)\n\nSafe and broad muscle delivery, due to low dose and low biodistribution to liver and spleen.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/69127bccf196dfeac65f9a8a_Icons-3.svg)\n\nTransduces **35-42% of NHP cardiac** cells at 1.6e13 vg/kg.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/69127bcebb53e8aeae3b9765_Icons-1.svg)\n\n**Confidence in human translation** given highly conserved entry receptor and *in vitro* transduction of human muscle cell lines.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6834c26dd42148723c30e214_gear.svg)\n\nEasily manufactured at a large scale and compatible with existing AAV9-based processes.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024b9f0b3e1eb90788fc9c_Group%201538240631.jpg)[View Presentation](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024c1a6995c269a0cc6084_ASGCT26-bn8_FINAL.pdf)\n\nMuscle/Neuromuscular\n\n## Dyno-n96\n\nLaunched at ASGCT 2026, the Dyno-n96 capsid enables therapeutic delivery to skeletal muscles at IV doses as low as 5e12 vg/kg, dramatically improving safety for muscle gene therapies.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024c85473b0519f94abc9a_Group%201538240399.png)\n\nLaunched at ASGCT 2026, the Dyno-n96 capsid enables therapeutic delivery to skeletal muscles at IV doses as low as 5e12 vg/kg, dramatically improving safety for muscle gene therapies.\n\n[\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024c66f2000929fc82883e_Group%201538240439.webp)\n\nExpand Image\n\n](#)\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024a0b4097b23f2d561e03_6962122362a4b74e399b8a8b_bar-chart%201.svg)\n\nAAVrh74-based, with stronger muscle transduction compared to other natural AAV serotypes.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024cc2f6398149a54eabe2_Icons.svg)\n\nEven at the low dose of 5e12 vg/kg (25x lower dose than Elevidys), transduces **74% of myofibers** in NHP skeletal muscles.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024cd1eedf7f88aaa900c6_Icons-1.svg)\n\nSafe and broad muscle delivery, due to low dose and low biodistribution to liver (1.4x < AAVrh74).\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024cce1e915771da61ab35_681e2c34cc117d9f87a1a80f_Icons%20from%20Figma%20(1)%201.svg)\n\n**Confidence in human translation** given *in vitro* transduction of human muscle cell lines.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024cd14bad77604662fe7f_Icons-2.svg)\n\nEasily manufactured at a large scale and compatible with existing AAV9-based processes.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a0251f4fec4b11009511ee3_Group%201538240637.png)[View Presentation](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a024d086247edc32f1280d1_ASGCT26-n96_FINAL.pdf)\n\nMuscle/Neuromuscular\n\n## Dyno-3hv\n\nLaunched in 2025, Dyno-3hv is the first capsid optimized for highly efficient delivery to the multiple tissues affected by neuromuscular disorders, including the heart, skeletal muscle and CNS.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2c15f9d68ca125ed3756_Group%20Design.png)\n\nLaunched in 2025, Dyno-3hv is the first capsid optimized for highly efficient delivery to the multiple tissues affected by neuromuscular disorders, including the heart, skeletal muscle and CNS.\n\n[\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/68221231f28b8364d2f72a83_3hvWebHisto.png)\n\nExpand Image\n\n](#)\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2c395e424f9372eb2dd3_Icons%20from%20Figma%20(2).svg)\n\nTransduces **50-90% of myofibers** in NHP skeletal muscles, and multiple regions of the heart and CNS at doses as low as 4e12 vg/kg.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2c452cc9592ca321a996_Group.svg)\n\nLow biodistribution to off-target peripheral organs, with **liver biodistribution <10 vg/dg** and **spleen <0.5 vg/dg** at a dose of 4e12 vg/kg, supporting safer IV dosing.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e29e99cac426cee799b23_syringe.svg)\n\n**Intravenous** injection enables more **uniform transduction** across cells and tissues and broader patient access.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2c34cc117d9f87a1a80f_Icons%20from%20Figma%20(1).svg)\n\n**Confidence in human translation** given highly conserved entry receptor and *in vitro* transduction of human muscle cell lines.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6834c26dd42148723c30e214_gear.svg)\n\n**Easily manufactured** at large scales and compatible with AAV9-based processes.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/69c1993c0b49083fde51b6e8_3hv.png)[View Presentation](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/682898a795f6e95d89f670fb_Web%20upload%20-%20ASGCT25%20Dyno-3hv%20-%20Compressed.pdf)\n\nEye\n\n## Dyno-4z2\n\nLaunched in 2025, Dyno-4z2 capsid is optimized for highly efficient delivery to the retina through intravitreal injection, with field-leading targeting of bipolar cells in the inner nuclear layer.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2930e84aa151ddc0e860_4z2.png)\n\nLaunched in 2025, Dyno-4z2 capsid is optimized for highly efficient delivery to the retina through intravitreal injection, with field-leading targeting of bipolar cells in the inner nuclear layer.\n\n[\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6822123d4cd7950d23aa937b_4z2WebHisto.png)\n\nExpand Image\n\n](#)\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2a183648022b23357734_eye.svg)\n\n**\\>40x** retinal transduction vs AAV2, **outperforms** all tested externally engineered capsids at doses of 1e10-1e11 vg/eye.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e29cf1816f58ee39e0e60_retina.svg)\n\nAn ideal capsid for **optogenetic** gene therapies**: 5x** transduction of **bipolar cells** in the **inner nuclear layer** compared to a reference externally engineered capsid.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e29e99cac426cee799b23_syringe.svg)\n\n**I****ntravitreal** injection enables easy administration and **broad patient access.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2a072d6950e8d6b250ac_primate.svg)\n\nOptimized and validated in **NHPs and mice,** supporting translation to humans.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6834c26dd42148723c30e214_gear.svg)\n\n**Easily manufactured** at large scales and compatible with AAV2-based processes.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/69c19953aef7ca5a5631cc07_4z2.png)[View Presentation](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/682796183c66c98161eafe10_Web%20upload%20-%20ASGCT25%20Dyno-4z2.pdf)\n\nEye\n\n## Dyno-86m\n\nLaunched in 2023, the Dyno-86m vector was the first Dyno ocular capsid optimized for easy and highly efficient delivery to the retina through intravitreal injection, with a broad retinal tropism.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2a8b05b8192f32e360f3_86m.png)\n\nLaunched in 2023, the Dyno-86m vector was the first Dyno ocular capsid optimized for easy and highly efficient delivery to the retina through intravitreal injection, with a broad retinal tropism.\n\n[\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2aa4d191d4245e9cddf5_Website%20Histology%20eCap%201.png)\n\nExpand Image\n\n](#)\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6834c26dd42148723c30e214_gear.svg)\n\n**80x** higher retinal transduction vs AAV2, with **similar production efficiency.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e29cf1816f58ee39e0e60_retina.svg)\n\nTransduces **retinal ganglion cells**, **bipolar cells** and **rod photoreceptors.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2a183648022b23357734_eye.svg)\n\nReaches **macula** and **peripheral retina**, enabling biofactory, neuroprotective, optogenetic and photoreceptor therapies.\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e29e99cac426cee799b23_syringe.svg)\n\nEasy **intravitreal** injection enables **broad patient access.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/681e2a072d6950e8d6b250ac_primate.svg)\n\nOptimized and validated in **NHPs.**\n\n![](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/69c1996aa510f73f0d38c923_86m.png)[View Presentation](https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6750826d5fe256d2ed79bd20/6a7b52e84727dc6facc7c8b0_Dyno-86m%20external%20deck.pdf)\n\n## Start collaborating with Dyno\n\nReach out to [partnerwith@dynotx.com](mailto:partnerwith@dynotx.com?subject=Start%20collaborating%20with%20Dyno) to learn how Dyno’s capsid platform can level-up your gene therapies.\n\n[](#)\n\n[](https://twitter.com/dyno_tx)[](https://www.linkedin.com/company/dynotx)\n\n343 Arsenal St  \nWatertown, MA 02472\n\n-   [Gene Delivery](/gene-delivery)\n    \n-   [Partnerships](/partnerships)\n    \n-   [Approach](/approach)\n    \n-   [About](/about)\n    \n-   [News](/news)\n    \n-   [Blog](https://dynotx.substack.com/)\n    \n-   [Careers](/careers)\n    \n-   [Frontiers Network](/frontiers-network)\n    \n-   [GATC 2026](/gatc2026)\n    \n\n© Dyno 2026\n\n[Privacy Policy](/legal/privacy-policy)[Terms + Conditions](/legal/terms-and-conditions)\n\nDyno Therapeutics, DYNO, the DYNO logo, and mountain design are registered trademarks of Dyno Therapeutics, Inc. All rights reserved."
